  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 9\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{P((3\\le X\\le 9),Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,Y=3)+P(X=6,Y=3)+P(X=9,Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)+f(9,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(3) & =f(0,3)+f(3,3)+f(6,3)+f(9,3) \\\\  & =0.05+0.1+0.2+0 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,3)=0.1,f(6,3)=0.2$ and $f(9,3)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 9\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)+f(9,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0.2+0}{0.35} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.3}{0.35} \\\\  & \u22480.86.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
